   "id": 545768,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "An average bath uses about 35 gal of water. A water-saving showerhead uses approximately 2 gal of water per minute. If a person typically takes one bath a week, how much water is saved by replacing the baths with showers lasting 5 minutes over the course of a month?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Find how much water is used by a five-minute shower that uses 2 gallons per minute.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"5{\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{minute}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{2{\\rm{\\ gallons}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{minute}}}}}}} \\right) = 10{\\rm{\\ gallons}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Find how much water is used by a shower a week for a month.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{10{\\rm{\\ gallons}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{shower}}}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{1\\cancel{{{\\rm{shower}}}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{week}}}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{4\\cancel{{{\\rm{weeks}}}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}} \\right) = \\frac{{40{\\rm{\\ gallons}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Find how many gallons used by a bath a week for a month.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{\\rm{35\\ gallons}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{bath}}}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{1\\cancel{{{\\rm{bath}}}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{week}}}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{4\\cancel{{{\\rm{weeks}}}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}} \\right) = \\frac{{140{\\rm{\\ gallons}}}}{{{\\rm{month}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Find the difference.</p>\n<p>140 – 40 = 100</p>\n<p>You save 100 gallons a month by using the water-saving showerhead and taking a five-minute shower once a week.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "100 gal"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
